<!--
    kuna lane division: a split whose lanes would give a free varnode two
    readers.  sub_e87b0 of Ubuntu 26.04's bash (package bash 5.3-2ubuntu1,
    amd64, /usr/bin/bash sha256
    3efccc187bafa75ff1e37d246270ab3e7aa559f242c7a52bf3ec2a1b5450bdbd), image
    bytes 0xe87b0..0xe9400; the function is 0x760 bytes and its flow reaches
    the code after it.

    Stage model: P3 dataflow, ActionLaneDivide over TransformManager
    (substrate/transform.rs).  No P0 assertion: a strict bug fix with no
    option.

    The bug.  The IMULs at 0xe898d (64-bit, 16-byte product) and
    0xe8bc2/0xe8d82 (32-bit, 8-byte product) compute their flags through the
    same unique temporary u0x5a200, so heritage carries the 16-byte temporary
    across blocks from an input at the entry.  Lane division traces it like a
    laned register, and its lanes, being unique storage, become temporaries
    that more than one op of the split reads.  TransformManager::apply only
    met that in placeInputs, after it had rewritten the function, so the
    function failed with "laned register split failed part way: Free varnode
    has multiple descendants" and the console aborted before any assertion.

    The fix.  check_free_fanout refuses the transform before anything is
    rewritten, and ActionLaneDivide counts the refusal as a failed trace.
    One pass, default pipeline.
-->
